$DIR/main.p:14:8: cannot store &x in the backing array of gv.Slice(), which outlives x
    &x points into x. x is a local variable of f (declared at main.p:12). When f
    returns, x's memory is reclaimed, but the backing array of gv.Slice() may be
    on the heap and live longer, so it would be left pointing at reclaimed
    memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of x, or allocate x with new(int) and store
    its owner, an owned[int], in the backing array of gv.Slice().
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)
